aac_adtstoasc: check the bit reader initialization before the PCE (CVE-2026-125225)

For an ADTS frame without a channel configuration the filter read the PCE through
a bit reader whose initialization it did not check; a packet too large for the
bit count left the reader on a NULL buffer.

Backport of FFmpeg master 3b1cbb5e0f66b85d15f1d3527436520b3f4711ec (PR 25569, merged 2026-11-03), not in n9.0.2.
Only the hunk line numbers differ from the master commit.

diff --git a/libavcodec/bsf/aac_adtstoasc.c b/libavcodec/bsf/aac_adtstoasc.c
--- a/libavcodec/bsf/aac_adtstoasc.c
+++ b/libavcodec/bsf/aac_adtstoasc.c
@@ -79,7 +79,9 @@ static int aac_adtstoasc_filter(AVBSFContext *bsfc, AVPacket *pkt)
 
         if (!hdr.chan_config) {
             GetBitContext gb;
-            init_get_bits(&gb, pkt->data, pkt->size * 8);
+            ret = init_get_bits8(&gb, pkt->data, pkt->size);
+            if (ret < 0)
+                goto fail;
             if (get_bits(&gb, 3) != 5) {
                 avpriv_report_missing_feature(bsfc,
                                               "PCE-based channel configuration "
